<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Warner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1580–<a href="/years/1649">1649</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Thomas Warner (c. 1580–1649) was an English captain who founded the first English colony in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> on Saint Christopher (St Kitts) in 1624. With French settlers he massacred the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a> in 1626 and divided the island with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. As governor he also sponsored English settlement of Nevis, Antigua and Montserrat.</p></div>
